IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `uc-core`
IMPORT `uc-core-bodies`

-- The Universal Credit Regulations 2013 (S.I. 2013/376), Schedule 1 (meaning of payments in respect of accommodation), paragraph 1: the definitions.
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/uksi-2013-376.txt, a plain-text rendering of the revised text (legislation.gov.uk, version 2026-07-16)
-- made by a converter script. It is not the official text. Every `-- src:N | ...` line copies line N of that file.
-- Target: the stable build 1.6.98. Layer 1: the law, objectively.
--
-- Each defined term that the text builds out of conditions is a rule over a record of the facts. A term that the text defines only by
-- pointing to another Act ("approved premises", "exempt accommodation", "housing association") or to regulation 26(6) ("shared ownership
-- tenancy") is a stated input wherever a later rule needs it (a field of the record that rule takes): the Acts are not among the inputs,
-- and regulation 26 is uc1's. The rows of the coverage table in NOTES.md say which.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- independent hospital: the test depends on the nation the hospital is in. Whether a hospital is one within the Act of that nation is a
-- stated input; the Acts are not among the inputs.
-- src:1833 | “independent hospital”—
-- src:1834 | (a) in England, means a hospital as defined by section 275 of the National Health Service Act 2006 that is not a health service hospital as defined by that section;
-- src:1835 | (b) in Wales, has the meaning assigned to it by section 2 of the Care Standards Act 2000 ;
-- src:1836 | (c) in Scotland, means an independent health care service as defined in section 10F(1)(a) and (b) of the National Health Service (Scotland) Act 1978 ;
@ref Sch 1 para 1 "independent hospital" (src:1833-1836)
DECLARE `Hospital that may be an independent hospital` HAS
    `a hospital as defined by section 275 of the National Health Service Act 2006`                                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `a health service hospital as defined by section 275 of the National Health Service Act 2006`                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `an independent hospital as the meaning is assigned to it by section 2 of the Care Standards Act 2000`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `an independent health care service as defined in section 10F(1)(a) and (b) of the National Health Service (Scotland) Act 1978`  IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:1833 | “independent hospital”—
-- src:1834 | (a) in England, means a hospital as defined by section 275 of the National Health Service Act 2006 that is not a health service hospital as defined by that section;
-- src:1835 | (b) in Wales, has the meaning assigned to it by section 2 of the Care Standards Act 2000 ;
-- src:1836 | (c) in Scotland, means an independent health care service as defined in section 10F(1)(a) and (b) of the National Health Service (Scotland) Act 1978 ;
@ref Sch 1 para 1 "independent hospital" (src:1833-1836)
GIVEN nation IS A `Nation of Great Britain`
      hospital IS A `Hospital that may be an independent hospital`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 1 para 1 — independent hospital` nation hospital MEANS
    CONSIDER nation
    WHEN England  THEN (hospital's `a hospital as defined by section 275 of the National Health Service Act 2006`) AND (NOT (hospital's `a health service hospital as defined by section 275 of the National Health Service Act 2006`))
    WHEN Wales    THEN hospital's `an independent hospital as the meaning is assigned to it by section 2 of the Care Standards Act 2000`
    WHEN Scotland THEN hospital's `an independent health care service as defined in section 10F(1)(a) and (b) of the National Health Service (Scotland) Act 1978`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- care home: one test for each nation (limbs (a), (aa) and (b)), and in any of the cases an independent hospital is included (limb (c)).
-- Limb (a) shows dots after "in England" (line 1827): words were repealed there, and what remains is quoted and encoded as printed.
-- src:1826 | “care home”—
-- src:1827 | (a) in England ..., means a care home within the meaning of section 3 of the Care Standards Act 2000 ;
-- src:1828 | (aa) in Wales, means a place at which a care home service within the meaning of Part 1 of the Regulation and Inspection of Social Care (Wales) Act 2016 is provided wholly or mainly to persons aged 18 or over;
-- src:1829 | (b) in Scotland, means a care home service within the meaning of paragraph 2 of Schedule 12 to the Public Services Reform (Scotland) Act 2010 ; and
-- src:1830 | (c) in any of the above cases, includes an independent hospital;
@ref Sch 1 para 1 "care home" (src:1826-1830)
DECLARE `Premises that may be a care home` HAS
    `nation of Great Britain in which the premises are`                                                                       IS A `Nation of Great Britain`
    `a care home within the meaning of section 3 of the Care Standards Act 2000`                                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `a place at which a care home service within the meaning of Part 1 of the Regulation and Inspection of Social Care (Wales) Act 2016 is provided wholly or mainly to persons aged 18 or over`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `a care home service within the meaning of paragraph 2 of Schedule 12 to the Public Services Reform (Scotland) Act 2010`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the premises as a hospital that may be an independent hospital`                                                          IS A `Hospital that may be an independent hospital`

-- src:1826 | “care home”—
-- src:1827 | (a) in England ..., means a care home within the meaning of section 3 of the Care Standards Act 2000 ;
-- src:1828 | (aa) in Wales, means a place at which a care home service within the meaning of Part 1 of the Regulation and Inspection of Social Care (Wales) Act 2016 is provided wholly or mainly to persons aged 18 or over;
-- src:1829 | (b) in Scotland, means a care home service within the meaning of paragraph 2 of Schedule 12 to the Public Services Reform (Scotland) Act 2010 ; and
-- src:1830 | (c) in any of the above cases, includes an independent hospital;
@ref Sch 1 para 1 "care home" (src:1826-1830)
GIVEN premises IS A `Premises that may be a care home`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 1 para 1 — care home` premises MEANS
    (`Sch 1 para 1 — care home, limbs (a), (aa) and (b)` premises)
    OR (`Sch 1 para 1 — independent hospital` (premises's `nation of Great Britain in which the premises are`) (premises's `the premises as a hospital that may be an independent hospital`))

-- src:1827 | (a) in England ..., means a care home within the meaning of section 3 of the Care Standards Act 2000 ;
-- src:1828 | (aa) in Wales, means a place at which a care home service within the meaning of Part 1 of the Regulation and Inspection of Social Care (Wales) Act 2016 is provided wholly or mainly to persons aged 18 or over;
-- src:1829 | (b) in Scotland, means a care home service within the meaning of paragraph 2 of Schedule 12 to the Public Services Reform (Scotland) Act 2010 ; and
@ref Sch 1 para 1 "care home" limbs (a), (aa) and (b) (src:1827-1829)
GIVEN premises IS A `Premises that may be a care home`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 1 para 1 — care home, limbs (a), (aa) and (b)` premises MEANS
    CONSIDER premises's `nation of Great Britain in which the premises are`
    WHEN England  THEN premises's `a care home within the meaning of section 3 of the Care Standards Act 2000`
    WHEN Wales    THEN premises's `a place at which a care home service within the meaning of Part 1 of the Regulation and Inspection of Social Care (Wales) Act 2016 is provided wholly or mainly to persons aged 18 or over`
    WHEN Scotland THEN premises's `a care home service within the meaning of paragraph 2 of Schedule 12 to the Public Services Reform (Scotland) Act 2010`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- registered charity: entered in either register.
-- src:1837 | “registered charity” means a charity entered in the register of charities maintained under Part 4 of the Charities Act 2011 or a body entered on the register of charities maintained under the Charities and Trustee Investment (Scotland) Act 2005 ;
@ref Sch 1 para 1 "registered charity" (src:1837)
DECLARE `Charity that may be a registered charity` HAS
    `entered in the register of charities maintained under Part 4 of the Charities Act 2011`                                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `entered on the register of charities maintained under the Charities and Trustee Investment (Scotland) Act 2005`              IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:1837 | “registered charity” means a charity entered in the register of charities maintained under Part 4 of the Charities Act 2011 or a body entered on the register of charities maintained under the Charities and Trustee Investment (Scotland) Act 2005 ;
@ref Sch 1 para 1 "registered charity" (src:1837)
GIVEN charity IS A `Charity that may be a registered charity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 1 para 1 — registered charity` charity MEANS
    (charity's `entered in the register of charities maintained under Part 4 of the Charities Act 2011`)
    OR (charity's `entered on the register of charities maintained under the Charities and Trustee Investment (Scotland) Act 2005`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- tent: a moveable structure designed or adapted (solely or mainly) for sleeping in, that is not a caravan, a mobile home or a houseboat.
-- src:1839 | “tent” means a moveable structure that is designed or adapted (solely or mainly) for the purpose of sleeping in a place for any period and that is not a caravan, a mobile home or a houseboat;
@ref Sch 1 para 1 "tent" (src:1839)
DECLARE `Structure that may be a tent` HAS
    `moveable structure`                                                                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `designed or adapted (solely or mainly) for the purpose of sleeping in a place for any period`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `caravan`                                                                                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `mobile home`                                                                                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `houseboat`                                                                                             IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:1839 | “tent” means a moveable structure that is designed or adapted (solely or mainly) for the purpose of sleeping in a place for any period and that is not a caravan, a mobile home or a houseboat;
@ref Sch 1 para 1 "tent" (src:1839)
GIVEN structure IS A `Structure that may be a tent`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 1 para 1 — tent` structure MEANS
    (structure's `moveable structure`)
    AND (structure's `designed or adapted (solely or mainly) for the purpose of sleeping in a place for any period`)
    AND (NOT ((structure's `caravan`) OR (structure's `mobile home`) OR (structure's `houseboat`)))

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- voluntary organisation: a body, other than a public or local authority, whose activities are carried on otherwise than for profit.
-- "Local authority" is regulation 2's definition (the keel's rule); a public authority is a stated input.
-- src:1841 | “voluntary organisation” means a body (other than a public or local authority) whose activities are carried on otherwise than for profit.
@ref Sch 1 para 1 "voluntary organisation" (src:1841)
DECLARE `Body that may be a voluntary organisation` HAS
    `public authority`                                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the body as a possible local authority`                                    IS A `Body that may be a local authority`
    `activities are carried on otherwise than for profit`                       IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:1841 | “voluntary organisation” means a body (other than a public or local authority) whose activities are carried on otherwise than for profit.
@ref Sch 1 para 1 "voluntary organisation" (src:1841)
GIVEN body IS A `Body that may be a voluntary organisation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 1 para 1 — voluntary organisation` body MEANS
    (NOT ((body's `public authority`) OR (`reg 2 — local authority` (body's `the body as a possible local authority`))))
    AND (body's `activities are carried on otherwise than for profit`)
